<section id="sequenceDiscovery"><h2>Swing sequence discovery</h2><p>Scan the selected start/end dates and chart timeframe. Counts use swing type, candle colours and wick geometry, independently of strategy filters.</p><div class="controls"><label>Swings per sequence<select id="sqLen"><option>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label><label>Maximum skipped pivots per step<select id="sqSkip"><option>0</option><option>1</option><option>2</option></select></label><label>Minimum occurrences<input id="sqMin" type="number" value="2" min="1"></label><label>Match swing labels<select id="sqType"><option value="relative">Relative: HH / HL / LH / LL / equal / initial</option><option value="broad">High / Low families (includes initial pivots)</option></select></label><label>Forward chart bars<input id="sqHorizon" type="number" min="1" max="200" value="30"></label><label>Break requires<select id="sqBasis"><option value="close">Close through level</option><option value="wick">Wick through level</option></select></label><label><input id="stEnable" type="checkbox">Test BUY and SELL trade scenarios</label><button id="sqRun">Run swing sequence report</button></div><details><summary>Trade scenario assumptions (only used if checked)</summary><div class="controls"><label>Entry scenarios<select id="stMode"><option value="all">All: break, return, post-break retest</option><option value="break">Break → next open</option><option value="return">Return to pivot OHLC after confirmation</option><option value="retest">Retest pivot OHLC after break</option></select></label><label>SL points<input id="stStop" type="number" step=".25" value="5"></label><label>TP points<input id="stTarget" type="number" step=".25" value="10"></label><label>USD per point per contract<input id="stPoint" type="number" value="20"></label><label>Contracts<input id="stQty" type="number" value="1"></label><label>Round-trip cost USD per contract<input id="stFee" type="number" step=".01" value="0"></label></div><small>Touch tests use the pivot candle’s original open, high, low and close at −1, 0 and +1 NQ tick. Both sides use the same theoretical touch price. No slippage; costs default to zero. Both barriers hit: stop first. Intrabar touch-fill targets require a close at/beyond target on that entry bar. Complete follow-up windows only; overlapping trials are independent. Best historical results are in-sample.</small></details><div id="stResult"></div><p id="sqStatus"></p><div id="sqPatterns"></div><strong id="sqPattern"></strong><div id="sqOutcomes"></div><div id="sqOcc"></div><div id="sqDetail"></div></section><section id="pairResearch"><strong>Consecutive swing forensics and strategy</strong><p>Preset: LH GR upper-wick retest → LL RG lower-wick retest. Mark the watch, then a later retest close.</p><div class="controls"></div><button type="button" id="pairRun">Run swing-pair backtest for selected dates</button></section><details id='releaseORB'><summary>Session opening ranges</summary><div class='controls'></div></details><small>Private OHLC research â€¢ stored Eastern timestamps â€¢ no external chart service</small><p><a href="compare.php" style="color:#8cc9ff">Compare days / compare weeks →</a></p><label style="width:220px">Session-open markers<select id="sessions" onchange="draw()"><option value="on">Show Tokyo / midnight / London / NY</option><option value="off">Hide markers</option></select></label>

